column name / table: potential usage  
• PUBLICATIONS."country_code": filter to United States patents (‘US’).  
• PUBLICATIONS."kind_code": identify B‑series grant type (filter = ‘B2’ for granted utility patents).  
• PUBLICATIONS."publication_date": restrict to grant years 2010‑2014 (20100101‑20141231).  
• PUBLICATIONS."filing_date": filing date needed to measure 30‑day window for forward citations.  
• PUBLICATIONS."citation": VARIANT that stores citation records; by flattening we can count how many later patents cite a focal one and look at their dates.  
• PUBLICATIONS."publication_number": join‑key across tables and final reporting field.  
• PUBLICATIONS."application_kind": be sure we look at utility patents (value ‘A’).  
• ABS_AND_EMB."publication_number": join with PUBLICATIONS to get text embeddings.  
• ABS_AND_EMB."embedding_v1": vector used to compute patent‑to‑patent similarity.  
• ABS_AND_EMB."title", ABS_AND_EMB."abstract": optional descriptive fields for quick inspection.  

Typical conditions  
• WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'  
• AND   t."kind_code"   = 'B2'  
• AND   t."publication_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20141231  
• (optionally) AND t."application_kind" = 'A'  

Below are 10 exploratory → increasingly complex Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows, all identifiers double‑quoted).

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at basic columns for US B2 patents granted 2010‑2014.  
SELECT 
  "publication_number",
  "filing_date",
  "publication_date",
  "kind_code",
  "country_code"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'
  AND "kind_code"   = 'B2'
  AND "publication_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20141231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Check distinct values that appear in "kind_code" for US patents.  
SELECT DISTINCT "kind_code"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Inspect different "application_kind" values to confirm utility‑patent marker.  
SELECT DISTINCT "application_kind"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Look inside the VARIANT "citation" object for one random US B2 patent.  
SELECT 
  t."publication_number",
  c.value AS "citation_record"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") c
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code"   = 'B2'
  AND t."publication_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20141231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Try to pull individual keys from the citation record to see date & citing number.  
SELECT 
  c.value:"cited_by"."publication_number"::STRING   AS "citing_pub_no",
  c.value:"cited_by"."date"::NUMBER                 AS "citing_date",
  t."publication_number"                            AS "focal_publication"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") c
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code"   = 'B2'
  AND t."publication_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20141231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Count forward citations that arrive within 30 days of filing for each patent (sample).  
SELECT 
  t."publication_number",
  COUNT(*) AS "fwd_cites_30d"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") c
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code"   = 'B2'
  AND t."publication_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20141231
  AND c.value:"cited_by"."date"::NUMBER  
        BETWEEN t."filing_date" AND (t."filing_date" + 30)
GROUP BY t."publication_number"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Within each filing year, find the patent having the maximum forward citations in 30 days (sample output).  
SELECT 
  YEAR(t."filing_date")         AS "filing_year",
  t."publication_number",
  COUNT(*)                      AS "fwd_cites_30d"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") c
WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
  AND t."kind_code"   = 'B2'
  AND t."publication_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20141231
  AND c.value:"cited_by"."date"::NUMBER  
        BETWEEN t."filing_date" AND (t."filing_date" + 30)
GROUP BY 1,2
QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY YEAR(t."filing_date") ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC) = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Retrieve embeddings for patents granted in 2012 for later similarity work.  
SELECT 
  e."publication_number",
  e."embedding_v1"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB e
JOIN PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS p
  ON e."publication_number" = p."publication_number"
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND YEAR(p."filing_date") = 2012
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Compute cosine‑like similarity (dot product) between a focal patent and others in same filing year 2012 (only 20 results preview).  
SELECT 
  focal."publication_number"             AS "focal_pub",
  other."publication_number"             AS "other_pub",
  DOT_PRODUCT(focal."embedding_v1", other."embedding_v1") AS "sim_score"
FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB focal
JOIN PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB other
  ON TRUE
WHERE focal."publication_number" = 'US‑XXXXXXXX‑B2'   -- replace with real focal pub #
  AND other."publication_number" <> focal."publication_number"
  AND YEAR( (SELECT "filing_date" FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS 
             WHERE "publication_number" = other."publication_number") ) = 2012
ORDER BY "sim_score" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) End‑to‑end: pick 2010‑2014 US B2 patent with most 30‑day forward citations, then surface the single most similar patent (any kind) from same filing year.  
WITH fwd_counts AS (
  SELECT 
    t."publication_number",
    t."filing_date",
    YEAR(t."filing_date")             AS "filing_year",
    COUNT(*)                          AS "fwd_cites_30d"
  FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS t,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."citation") c
  WHERE t."country_code" = 'US'
    AND t."kind_code"   = 'B2'
    AND t."publication_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20141231
    AND c.value:"cited_by"."date"::NUMBER  
          BETWEEN t."filing_date" AND (t."filing_date" + 30)
  GROUP BY 1,2,3
  ORDER BY "fwd_cites_30d" DESC
  LIMIT 1
), all_same_year AS (
  SELECT 
    e."publication_number",
    e."embedding_v1"
  FROM PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB e
  JOIN PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.PUBLICATIONS p
    ON e."publication_number" = p."publication_number"
  JOIN fwd_counts f
    ON YEAR(p."filing_date") = f."filing_year"
)
SELECT 
  f."publication_number"                             AS "max_cited_patent",
  s."publication_number"                             AS "most_similar_patent",
  DOT_PRODUCT(f_emb."embedding_v1", s."embedding_v1") AS "similarity_score"
FROM fwd_counts f
JOIN PATENTS_GOOGLE.PATENTS_GOOGLE.ABS_AND_EMB f_emb
  ON f."publication_number" = f_emb."publication_number"
JOIN all_same_year s
  ON TRUE
WHERE s."publication_number" <> f."publication_number"
ORDER BY "similarity_score" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

Each query is capped at 20 rows and quoted according to Snowflake requirements.
